1
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:07,222
Hi! Welcome to TrainTanmay. I'm going to give you a quick tour,

2
00:00:07,172 --> 00:00:09,738
so you can get the most out of your revision.

3
00:00:10,338 --> 00:00:12,936
TrainTanmay is a set of free revision apps,

4
00:00:12,886 --> 00:00:15,722
made by an A level student, for other students.

5
00:00:16,198 --> 00:00:19,196
Each world on the start screen is its own app:

6
00:00:19,146 --> 00:00:23,106
Design & Technology, Physics, Chemistry, Maths, and the ESAT.

7
00:00:23,655 --> 00:00:26,805
Just pick a world to jump in. Let's start with Chemistry.

8
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:31,008
Every app works in a similar way.

9
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:32,957
The home page shows your progress,

10
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:36,052
the flashcards you've got due, and where you left off.

11
00:00:36,601 --> 00:00:39,835
Along the top, you'll find the notes, practice questions,

12
00:00:39,785 --> 00:00:41,287
past papers, and the labs.

13
00:00:41,837 --> 00:00:45,370
To switch apps, tap the TrainTanmay logo in the top corner.

14
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:49,031
Its colour tells you which app you're in: orange is Chemistry.

15
00:00:49,605 --> 00:00:52,556
Looking for something specific? Use Jump to anything,

16
00:00:52,506 --> 00:00:54,089
and just type what you need.

17
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:58,891
Every topic has full notes with worked examples, plus key terms,

18
00:00:58,841 --> 00:01:01,117
equations, flashcards, and videos.

19
00:01:01,668 --> 00:01:04,807
The notes were written with AI, so if anything looks off,

20
00:01:04,757 --> 00:01:07,462
double-check it against your textbook or a video.

21
00:01:08,266 --> 00:01:11,346
The calculation drills give you new numbers every time.

22
00:01:11,296 --> 00:01:13,990
Type your answer, and it's marked straight away,

23
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,257
with a worked solution.

24
00:01:15,809 --> 00:01:18,962
And in the labs, you can spin real 3D molecules,

25
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:22,969
see every bond angle, then flip it into an exam-style drawing.

26
00:01:23,719 --> 00:01:27,867
Design & Technology covers the whole Edexcel Product Design course.

27
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:30,741
Flip a flashcard, then say whether you knew it,

28
00:01:30,691 --> 00:01:33,066
and it'll come back at the right time.

29
00:01:33,518 --> 00:01:36,905
Physics has notes, practice tests, and nearly fifty labs,

30
00:01:36,855 --> 00:01:39,657
like this one, which flies real space missions.

31
00:01:40,118 --> 00:01:43,305
In Maths, you can search thousands of past papers,

32
00:01:43,255 --> 00:01:47,007
topic packs and worksheets, all sorted by course and topic.

33
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:50,744
And the ESAT app has real admissions test questions,

34
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:54,050
timed mocks, and analytics that show your weak spots.

35
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,795
Plus a few games, for when you need a break.

36
00:01:57,250 --> 00:02:00,656
Your progress saves automatically, right here in your browser.

37
00:02:00,606 --> 00:02:02,064
You don't need an account.

38
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:05,652
From Save progress, you can download a backup file,

39
00:02:05,602 --> 00:02:07,527
and load it again on any device.

40
00:02:08,077 --> 00:02:09,458
Or, sign in with Google,

41
00:02:09,408 --> 00:02:12,619
and your progress follows you to your phone, your laptop,

42
00:02:12,569 --> 00:02:14,006
and your school computer.

43
00:02:14,555 --> 00:02:16,536
Syncing only ever adds progress,

44
00:02:16,486 --> 00:02:19,313
so nothing on one device can wipe out another.

45
00:02:19,851 --> 00:02:23,262
Now for the fun part. Study leagues are weekly leaderboards,

46
00:02:23,212 --> 00:02:24,663
for you and your friends.

47
00:02:25,212 --> 00:02:27,444
They count your active revision minutes,

48
00:02:27,394 --> 00:02:29,953
whenever you're clicking, typing or scrolling,

49
00:02:29,903 --> 00:02:30,989
in any of the apps.

50
00:02:31,539 --> 00:02:33,770
Share your league code to invite people.

51
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,005
You can be in up to five leagues at once.

52
00:02:36,555 --> 00:02:38,545
Everyone's minutes reset on Monday,

53
00:02:38,495 --> 00:02:40,817
so there's a new crown to win every week.

54
00:02:41,368 --> 00:02:44,675
To start your own league, or join a friend's, tap New or join.

55
00:02:45,317 --> 00:02:46,974
Everyone reads differently.

56
00:02:46,924 --> 00:02:49,771
Tap the Aa button for a dyslexia-friendly font.

57
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,887
The menu next to it switches the colours. Try dark mode,

58
00:02:53,837 --> 00:02:55,835
or a softer, warmer background.

59
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:57,657
And in the logo menu,

60
00:02:57,607 --> 00:03:00,685
you can read everything in Welsh or Scottish Gaelic.

61
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:05,095
If you spot a mistake, or something's broken, tap Report a bug,

62
00:03:05,045 --> 00:03:07,265
and let Tanmay know. It really helps.

63
00:03:07,762 --> 00:03:10,170
That's everything! Good luck with your revision,

64
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,939
and I'll see you on the leaderboard.

